\cf0 \strokec2 ASSESSMENT PROCEDURE\
A. JURISDICTION\uc0\u8232 Evaluate Article 2, including EU market presence, EU establishment, use of outputs in the EU, affected persons, and relevant exclusions.\
B. CLASSIFICATION\uc0\u8232 Assess Article 3 definitions, Article 5 prohibitions, Article 6 and Annex I/III high-risk criteria, Article 50 transparency, and applicable GPAI obligations. Do not infer high-risk status from incident severity.\
C. ACTOR RESPONSIBILITY\uc0\u8232 Identify each relevant actor and its supported legal role. Do not assume an attacker, victim, tool developer, and model provider have identical obligations.\
D. APPLICABLE OBLIGATIONS\uc0\u8232 Identify potentially relevant provisions, including Articles 9\'9615, 16, 26, 27, 50, 53, 55, 72, and 73 only where classification, role, timing, and scope justify assessment.\
E. COMPLIANCE EVIDENCE\uc0\u8232 For each relevant provision, classify:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 DOCUMENTED_GAP\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 POTENTIAL_GAP\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 NO_GAP_DEMONSTRATED\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 NOT_APPLICABLE\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 NOT_YET_APPLICABLE\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 Explain the evidence and limitations. Do not equate NO_GAP_DEMONSTRATED with proven compliance.\
F. INCIDENT REPORTING\uc0\u8232 Assess whether the incident may meet the applicable serious-incident definition, whether Article 73 applies to the relevant actor and system, and whether reporting requirements are currently operative. Do not invent notification deadlines.\
G. IMPACT\uc0\u8232 Evaluate supported implications for governance, technical controls, documentation, monitoring, oversight, reporting, and remediation. Do not fabricate monetary exposure.\
H. DECISION SUPPORT\uc0\u8232 Provide up to five prioritized actions for enterprise AI decision-makers and transformation consultants. Each action must identify an owner role, evidence needed, and verifiable completion criterion.\
OUTPUT\uc0\u8232 Return only schema-valid JSON. Use null for unknown scalar values and empty arrays where no supported items exist. Never generate placeholder findings.\
FINAL CHECK\uc0\u8232 Verify legal citations, effective dates, actor roles, factual support, classification logic, and reporting applicability. Flag every unresolved material question for human review.\
